{"event_type":"review","id":"b9f481a3da46784f421c74641f11ab96de73badb7be0ba45667c941809db5b48","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T19:38:18Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/2ace9c02139dcc9b70c553ad8dfbd627521b2cd710efaa61ba776fc5e2ccfa5c","sha256":"2ace9c02139dcc9b70c553ad8dfbd627521b2cd710efaa61ba776fc5e2ccfa5c"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5270000a1a313cc471bcd014614789cb71c7c439f849c6cc2f412026c9b2d4bb","sha256":"5270000a1a313cc471bcd014614789cb71c7c439f849c6cc2f412026c9b2d4bb"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3b0c670d6865ae40a9a68df8684e1ce5742728269dbbe9602db761dcf48e40ef","sha256":"3b0c670d6865ae40a9a68df8684e1ce5742728269dbbe9602db761dcf48e40ef"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f7345a28b52ef3b52aa8dd7da5f0692d21a9e4d2cb39fed61811d0b118d43129","sha256":"f7345a28b52ef3b52aa8dd7da5f0692d21a9e4d2cb39fed61811d0b118d43129"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/205f743aee6d79aa204f5f472fc379b86fac6894dfe35b23ee9cc7142f50a4a1","sha256":"205f743aee6d79aa204f5f472fc379b86fac6894dfe35b23ee9cc7142f50a4a1"}],"attempt_id":"b06438ab415a3a0f49b419a1d688e0d25ccd2e2b05d1b1c89edac5832a0cdbda:0:1","base":"028b25f6f16e5bdd94674da0445b25769bb6299e","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"6cf8902f43171da3ffb16e0856b32e15f4ca6f68","body":"**Unquoted `$RANGE` and an empty-range edge case in the octopus-merge loop.**\n\nAt `.github/workflows/denylist.yml:85`, `git rev-list --min-parents=3 \"$RANGE\"` receives the quoted range, so the shell does not split it. This works. On the default branch with `base=\"\"`, the range is `HEAD`, which scans all history. That is intended.\n\nFor the loop on Lines 85-87, `$(git rev-list ...)` feeds a `for` loop. With `set -e`, a `git rev-list` failure inside the command substitution does not abort the step. The loop then runs zero times, and octopus merges go unscanned. The step would still pass. Read the commits into a variable first, so a failure aborts the step.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-          for commit in $(git rev-list --min-parents=3 \"$RANGE\"); do\n+          octopus=$(git rev-list --min-parents=3 \"$RANGE\")\n+          for commit in $octopus; do\n```\n</details>\n\nAn assignment propagates the exit status under `set -e`, so a failed `git rev-list` fails the step. The required check no longer passes with unscanned octopus merges.","id":"5f34fddbf21e50a4e8e67b03b63b5fe20ded4ff1f3dbdd04735e276ee7d2fb4e","intervals":[],"path":".github/workflows/denylist.yml","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Unquoted `$RANGE` and an empty-range edge case in the octopus-merge loop."}],"head":"cc7c15d951f9c3b1dedcb423dd5d854f42e4f431","head_tree":"067d49da10942551a3c39da201ad1d79467f9afa","input_scope":[{"blob":"6cf8902f43171da3ffb16e0856b32e15f4ca6f68","intervals":[[1,94]],"path":".github/workflows/denylist.yml"}],"job_id":"b06438ab415a3a0f49b419a1d688e0d25ccd2e2b05d1b1c89edac5832a0cdbda:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"6cf8902f43171da3ffb16e0856b32e15f4ca6f68","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":".github/workflows/denylist.yml","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"6cf8902f43171da3ffb16e0856b32e15f4ca6f68","intervals":[[5,8],[24,27],[29,45],[84,84],[86,86],[94,94]],"path":".github/workflows/denylist.yml"}],"reviewed_scope":[{"blob":"6cf8902f43171da3ffb16e0856b32e15f4ca6f68","intervals":[[5,8],[24,27],[29,45],[84,84],[86,86],[94,94]],"path":".github/workflows/denylist.yml"}],"scope_digest":"32b657e30e54f2104f67bb8